The odds of the *first* gift at sacrifice are not effected at
all by the number of existing artifacts.  Which first gift
you get is limited to ones that do not already exist but
the odds aren't effected.  Thus you can still get an artifact
through sacrifice.

Priests don't have a specific first artifact so that isn't as
limited by existing artifacts.

It's the second and subsequent artifact gift that gets worse
odds.  The formula has the number of sacrifice gifts times
the number of existing artifacts on the bottom - It goes
sorta by the inverse square of the existing artifacts but not
quite.

